content.text:
Light hero: stats are readable but "0 file" and "Gratis" are over the art page card (semi-transparent). The middle stat "0 file ke server" has the card behind, reducing contrast but still readable. Visually a bit cluttered. The page cards also overlap the CTA? The front page card top-left starts below CTA (y≈340) and CTA at 375? Actually front card starts at y=337 and CTA ends 394; the card overlaps right of CTA area but CTA width 125 ends x=148; card at x=245; no.

To improve, we can make the art pages more transparent on mobile (already .72 opacity) and add a backdrop behind stats. Perhaps `.hero-stats` with a `background:linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(...))`? Or simply reduce art height/opacity at mobile to 0.5. Stats over gradient still slightly visible. The main problem is the middle stat behind a page. Give stats z-index + text-shadow not enough. Add a soft "glass" strip behind stats:
```
@media(max-width:860px){.hero-stats{padding:5px 8px;border-radius:9px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.55);backdrop-filter:blur(6px)}}
body dark .hero-stats{background:rgba(31,37,52,.55)}
```
But the stats are positioned at left 23 bottom 14; adding background and padding might make them look like a chip, could be a nice UI. It would also increase height/width; check fit: stats width 243 + padding 16 = 259; left 23 → ends 282 < 390. Constrain. The background masks the art behind stats, improving readability. On mobile, hero art still visible around. This is a reasonable UI improvement.

Alternatively move page cards above stats: set mobile `.hero-art{bottom:34px}` so not overlapping vertical. Art height 145 bottom 34 → top at hero height -179 = 117, pages top 11+117=128; they'd overlap copy text (body at 320?). Copy is at top 100-180; art starts 128 → overlap copy. But art is right; copy max width 310 of 344; overlap. No.

Set stats background. Also increase z-index.

At 768 mobile, stats background would also appear; could look okay. Maybe only max480 to target phones. Use `@media(max-width:480px)`.

```
@media(max-width:480px){
 .hero-stats{z-index:3;padding:4px 7px;border-radius:8px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.62);backdrop-filter:blur(5px);box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(...);bottom:12px}
 body[data-theme=dark] .hero-stats{background:rgba(33,40,58,.6)}
}
```
Need adjust stats left maybe 23; width 243+14=257; fits 344. Gap between stats items stays 9. The background will cover art; good. Could also reduce opacity to .65 to blend.

Would padding affect hero bottom fit? Stats height 25+8=33, bottom12; hero bottom; fine. But our earlier overlap checks measured CTA vs stats top; stats top rises by 8 (padding) maybe clamp gap. At 390, CTA bottom 408? Wait mobile earlier gap 63, plenty. At 320 gap 46. fine.

Add and check.

